# General Rules for Cursor AI

## Rule Structure
The rules folder is organized into categories:
- `core/`: Foundation rules governing overall system behavior
- `frontend/`: Rules specific to frontend development
- `backend/`: Rules specific to backend development
- `commands/`: Task automation commands organized by category (ops, service, task, web)
- `templates/`: Reusable templates for various components and structures
Each rule is defined in an MDC file with a specific purpose and is loaded based on context or explicitly fetched.

## Temporary Files and Scripts
All temporary files, scripts, test files, and experimental code MUST be created strictly within the `.tmp` folder at the root of the project. This includes:
- Test scripts
- Experimental code snippets
- Debugging files
- One-off utility scripts
- Generated test data
- Draft implementations
This folder is excluded from version control and deployments. Never place temporary files elsewhere in the codebase.

